<title>UK: Capel cuts Utd Utilities, Wessex.</title>
<headline>Capel cuts Utd Utilities, Wessex.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in utility companies United Utilities and Wessex Water fell on Monday after analysts at HSBC James Capel cut their rating on the stock to &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;hold&quot;, market sources said.</p>
<p>Shares in United were 11-1/2p lower at 692p whilst Wessex fell 6-1/2p to 472-1/2p by 0910 GMT.  </p>
<p>In a review of the sector the analysts were said to be recommending switching out of the two utilities which were seen to be overvalued, the sources said.</p>
<p>Their preferred stock in the sector was thought to be British Energy which was unchanged at 170-1/2p.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
